# Claude Code agent worktrees and local session state. These are live git
# worktrees, so committing them would add unresolvable gitlinks to the tree.
.claude/
# Signed-receipt logs written by local agent tool hooks. They record which tool
# calls a session made, not repository content, and they are rewritten on every
# call -- so an ignored path here is what keeps the governance worktree scan
# reporting real unknown paths instead of this session's own exhaust.
#
# Deliberately unanchored. The hook writes into the working directory of the
# tool call, not the repository root, so a command run from any subdirectory
# leaves a copy there and the unknown-path gate fails on the session's own
# exhaust -- the exact outcome these two lines exist to prevent. No tracked path
# uses either directory name.
receipts/
review-receipts/
